        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0,
          "end": 2.46,
          "en": "-: In this video, let's talk about tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.46,
          "end": 4.53,
          "en": "Now what is tag? We'll talk about that later.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.53,
          "end": 7.38,
          "en": "But before that I just want to show you one more thing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.38,
          "end": 9.3,
          "en": "which is about this remote.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 9.3,
          "end": 10.8,
          "en": "Now if you remember in the earlier video,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 10.8,
          "end": 12.21,
          "en": "we have done this push, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 12.21,
          "end": 14.43,
          "en": "So from the local machine, we were able",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 14.43,
          "end": 16.32,
          "en": "to send the data to this server, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 16.32,
          "end": 18.66,
          "en": "So basically we were able to push it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 18.66,
          "end": 20.07,
          "en": "Now it has four things.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 20.07,
          "end": 21.99,
          "en": "First of all, we have a git command of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 21.99,
          "end": 23.61,
          "en": "because we're using Git tool.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 23.61,
          "end": 27.24,
          "en": "Next we have push. Basically we are pushing the code, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 27.24,
          "end": 28.74,
          "en": "Or whatever data you have.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 28.74,
          "end": 31.5,
          "en": "And then we have something called an origin here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 31.5,
          "end": 32.82,
          "en": "Okay, so we'll talk about origin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 32.82,
          "end": 34.71,
          "en": "because that's very important for this part.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 34.71,
          "end": 36.6,
          "en": "Then we have, we are specifying the branch name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 36.6,
          "end": 38.49,
          "en": "So it can be main, it can be master,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 38.49,
          "end": 40.71,
          "en": "or any other branch which you create.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 40.71,
          "end": 42,
          "en": "Let's talk about this origin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 42,
          "end": 44.13,
          "en": "Why it has to be always origin?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 44.13,
          "end": 45.51,
          "en": "Of course we have done origin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 45.51,
          "end": 47.61,
          "en": "but it can be different as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 47.61,
          "end": 49.65,
          "en": "The thing is for this particular repository,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 49.65,
          "end": 51.36,
          "en": "what we have done is,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 51.36,
          "end": 54.24,
          "en": "when we talked about the remote server, we only have one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 54.24,
          "end": 59.1,
          "en": "Example, if I say git remote -v,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 59.1,
          "end": 60.27,
          "en": "so this is the command using,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 60.27,
          "end": 62.88,
          "en": "which you can see which is your origin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 62.88,
          "end": 65.28,
          "en": "So we can have a origin for fetch.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 65.28,
          "end": 66.66,
          "en": "So from the server to client,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 66.66,
          "end": 68.25,
          "en": "this is the link we have to use.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 68.25,
          "end": 70.89,
          "en": "And from client to server, again, we have the same link,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 70.89,
          "end": 73.23,
          "en": "because we only have one remote repo there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 73.23,
          "end": 74.94,
          "en": "And by default the name is origin.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 74.94,
          "end": 77.64,
          "en": "Of course this can be any name. You can change it as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 77.64,
          "end": 79.92,
          "en": "So you can rename it or you can connect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 79.92,
          "end": 81.81,
          "en": "to different repositories, not just one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 81.81,
          "end": 83.07,
          "en": "And you can pull and push",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 83.07,
          "end": 85.08,
          "en": "to any other repositories if you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 85.08,
          "end": 85.913,
          "en": "The only thing you have to do is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 85.913,
          "end": 87,
          "en": "you have to change this one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 87,
          "end": 88.59,
          "en": "So instead of pushing it to origin,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 88.59,
          "end": 90.18,
          "en": "you can push it to somewhere else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 90.18,
          "end": 92.72999999999999,
          "en": "Okay, so keeping that aside now, let's talk about tags.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 92.72999999999999,
          "end": 95.49000000000001,
          "en": "Now basically we have a concept of tagging.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 95.49000000000001,
          "end": 98.19,
          "en": "Now if you have observed, every software which we use,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 98.19,
          "end": 99.18,
          "en": "it has a version number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 99.18,
          "end": 101.16,
          "en": "Example, I'm using VS Code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 101.16,
          "end": 102.72,
          "en": "And if I go to Help",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 102.72,
          "end": 106.89,
          "en": "and if I click on, not Help here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 106.89,
          "end": 109.28999999999999,
          "en": "because in Windows, you will get that in Help.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 109.28999999999999,
          "end": 111.87,
          "en": "In Mac, you will get that in the About.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 111.87,
          "end": 114.42,
          "en": "So if you go to About VS Code here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 114.42,
          "end": 116.97,
          "en": "so you can see it is giving you a version number here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 116.97,
          "end": 119.49000000000001,
          "en": "So every time you download a software,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 119.49000000000001,
          "end": 121.02,
          "en": "you will get a particular version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 121.02,
          "end": 123.12,
          "en": "Of course you will also get the updates for it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 123.12,
          "end": 126.6,
          "en": "So you can simply go here and I can check for the updates.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 126.6,
          "end": 128.19,
          "en": "So you can see it says restart to update,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 128.19,
          "end": 129.6,
          "en": "but I don't want to restart now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 129.6,
          "end": 131.34,
          "en": "But you will also get update there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 131.34,
          "end": 134.52,
          "en": "So this is the current version, and this is a commit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 134.52,
          "end": 135.69,
          "en": "Now this looks weird, right?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 135.69,
          "end": 138.03,
          "en": "Why do we have a commit in the About?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 138.03,
          "end": 139.44,
          "en": "That, we'll see in sometime.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 139.44,
          "end": 141.57,
          "en": "And also observe some things, because in the next video,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 141.57,
          "end": 143.34,
          "en": "we'll talk about this thing in detail.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 143.34,
          "end": 145.44,
          "en": "Okay, so we have Electron, we have Chromium,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 145.44,
          "end": 147.9,
          "en": "we have Node.js, and all these have versions, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 147.9,
          "end": 149.13,
          "en": "So we'll talk about it in some time.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 149.13,
          "end": 151.35,
          "en": "But important is we have a version here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 151.35,
          "end": 154.17000000000002,
          "en": "Now this version is basically a tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 154.17000000000002,
          "end": 155.88,
          "en": "So let's say if you are working on a project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 158.1,
          "en": "and then you have done several commits,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 158.1,
          "end": 160.47,
          "en": "and now you think, okay, I'm all set",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 160.47,
          "end": 161.73,
          "en": "to release my next version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 161.73,
          "end": 163.62,
          "en": "So you can give a tag to it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 163.62,
          "end": 165.81,
          "en": "And then once that version is done,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 165.81,
          "end": 167.67000000000002,
          "en": "you can go for the next version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 167.67000000000002,
          "end": 168.84,
          "en": "So basically how do you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 168.84,
          "end": 171.42000000000002,
          "en": "give this tag, the version number, to each commit?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 171.42000000000002,
          "end": 172.95,
          "en": "So not exactly each commit,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 172.95,
          "end": 174.75,
          "en": "let's say you have done 10 commits",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 174.75,
          "end": 175.8,
          "en": "and then now you think, \"Okay,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 175.8,
          "end": 177,
          "en": "the software is up and running,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 177,
          "end": 179.82,
          "en": "we can publish this particular product to the users.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 179.82,
          "end": 181.26,
          "en": "We can give it a tag.\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 181.26,
          "end": 182.093,
          "en": "First of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 182.093,
          "end": 185.55,
          "en": "how do I check how many tags I have for this project?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 185.55,
          "end": 186.87,
          "en": "Now the way you can do that is",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 186.87,
          "end": 189.239,
          "en": "by using something called git tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 189.239,
          "end": 192.15,
          "en": "And when you say Enter, it will show you all the tags",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 192.15,
          "end": 194.01,
          "en": "which you have given to till now for this project.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 194.01,
          "end": 197.22,
          "en": "And this is empty, it's because we have not given any tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 197.22,
          "end": 199.56,
          "en": "So let's give our first tag here. How will I do that?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 199.56,
          "end": 202.62,
          "en": "It's very simple. You can say git tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 202.62,
          "end": 205.14,
          "en": "And then when you say tagging, there are two options here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 205.14,
          "end": 207.12,
          "en": "One, you can use annotated tagging",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 207.12,
          "end": 209.25,
          "en": "or you can use lightweight tagging.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 209.25,
          "end": 212.07,
          "en": "Now if you really want to release this to the users",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 212.07,
          "end": 214.86,
          "en": "and if you want to give more information about the user,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 214.86,
          "end": 218.34,
          "en": "I mean who is committing it or who owns it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 218.34,
          "end": 222.15,
          "en": "so if you want all those information, use annotated, okay?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 222.15,
          "end": 223.29,
          "en": "Otherwise you can go for lightweight,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 223.29,
          "end": 224.34,
          "en": "which you're not going to see.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 224.34,
          "end": 227.34,
          "en": "So let's see, annotated here, where every version",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 227.34,
          "end": 229.41,
          "en": "will have different information about it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 229.41,
          "end": 233.91,
          "en": "So for that, we have to use a -a as a option",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 233.91,
          "end": 234.96,
          "en": "for the annotated one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 234.96,
          "end": 237.21,
          "en": "And then now you can mention your tag number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 237.21,
          "end": 238.62,
          "en": "So basically these are your version numbers.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 238.62,
          "end": 240.81,
          "en": "So there are different ways of using version number.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 240.81,
          "end": 244.38,
          "en": "Some people simply go with 1.0, like this version.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 244.38,
          "end": 245.91,
          "en": "Or you can also mention v here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 245.91,
          "end": 248.76,
          "en": "So v1.0, so we can go",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 248.76,
          "end": 250.95,
          "en": "with this particular one which is v1.0,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 250.95,
          "end": 253.53,
          "en": "this is our version which we are specifying here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 253.53,
          "end": 255.96,
          "en": "And then you can also provide a message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 255.96,
          "end": 259.26,
          "en": "In fact, we need to do that, otherwise, Git will open a data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 259.26,
          "end": 260.34,
          "en": "where you have to mention this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 260.34,
          "end": 263.22,
          "en": "otherwise, let's say -m to give the message,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 263.22,
          "end": 266.58,
          "en": "and I can say first release.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 266.58,
          "end": 268.5,
          "en": "So you can give something like this as a message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 268.5,
          "end": 270.69,
          "en": "And when you say Enter, now tagging is done.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 270.69,
          "end": 272.49,
          "en": "So you got the first tag.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 272.49,
          "end": 274.89,
          "en": "Now if you want to check, you can say git tag again.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 274.89,
          "end": 276.72,
          "en": "And you can see we got one tag here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 276.72,
          "end": 279.9,
          "en": "And of course you can also see detailed information.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 279.9,
          "end": 282.447,
          "en": "So you can say git show v1.0.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 282.447,
          "end": 284.52,
          "en": "Now this will give you description",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 284.52,
          "end": 286.08,
          "en": "about this particular tag.",
          "zh": ""
